  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "r20261118-a01",
      "title": "Saturday Night at the Market",
      "level": "Dasar",
      "min": 2,
      "body": [
        "Every Saturday night, the street near Tania's house becomes a night market. Colorful lights hang above the road, and the air smells like grilled corn and satay.",
        "Tania goes there with her grandmother. First, they buy a bag of sweet mangoes. Then Tania watches a man make candy from melted sugar. He shapes it like butterflies and dragons. \"Can I have the dragon?\" Tania asks. It costs five thousand rupiah.",
        "At the end of the night, grandmother buys warm ginger tea for both of them. They walk home slowly, full and happy. \"Same time next week?\" her grandmother says. Tania nods and smiles."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "night market": "pasar malam",
        "hang": "tergantung",
        "grilled": "dibakar",
        "candy": "permen",
        "melted": "dilelehkan",
        "shapes": "membentuk",
        "ginger tea": "teh jahe",
