    {
      "id": "r20261118-a02",
      "title": "The Secret Life of Honeybees",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "A honeybee lives only about six weeks, but it works every single day. In that short life, one bee makes just a twelfth of a teaspoon of honey. A full jar of honey needs the work of hundreds of bees.",
        "Bees are also amazing communicators. When a bee finds flowers, it flies home and does a special dance. The angle of the dance tells the other bees which direction to fly, and its speed tells them how far to go.",
        "Sadly, bee numbers are falling around the world. Chemicals on farms hurt them, and cities leave fewer wild flowers. This is a problem for us too: about a third of our food depends on bees. Planting flowers on balconies and in gardens is a small way to help."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "teaspoon": "sendok teh",
        "jar": "toples",
        "communicators": "penyampai pesan",
        "dance": "tarian",
        "direction": "arah",
        "falling": "menurun",
        "chemicals": "bahan kimia",
        "depends on": "bergantung pada"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "How much honey does one bee make in its life?",
          "opts": [
            "About one jar",
            "About one cup",
            "About a twelfth of a teaspoon"
          ],
          "a": 2
        },
        {
          "q": "How does a bee tell others where the flowers are?",
          "opts": [
            "By making a loud sound",
            "By doing a special dance",
            "By leaving a smell"
          ],
          "a": 1
        },
        {
          "q": "Why are falling bee numbers a problem for humans?",
          "opts": [
